      "title": "SW - Campus Ministry Student Minister",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-20\n\nLocation: Honolulu\n\nCHAMINADE UNIVERSITY OF HONOLULU   Position Information Title: Campus Ministry Student Minister Division: Vice President for Mission / Rector Department: Campus Ministry Non-Exempt Part time Position Summary The Student Minister serves as an ambassador of CUH Campus Ministry to other students, prospective students, and other departments, offices and student organizations. They invite, recruit and engage students in faith programs, design and post vibrant communications, and bring a student perspective to Campus Ministry event planning. Essential tasks include reaching out to and inviting students to CM events, designing flyers and social media posts, and collaborating with other university departments and student organizations. They represent Campus Ministry at various events and also assist in routine tasks of the CM department. Learning Outcomes  (what will the student learn from this job? Consider  transferable  skills for their future career) The Campus Ministry Student Minister will learn: 1.Effective methods of communicating and recruiting others to voluntary events.  2. Event planning skills, from visioning to implementation to evaluation/assessment. 3. Basic principles and best practices of professional campus ministry from a Catholic Christian perspective. 4. To build skills and proficiency in digital creation and editing.  5. Collaborative planning and working as part of a team. Reports to: Direct Report to: The Director of Campus Ministry.  Indirect Report to: Daily tasks will often be communicated to this position through the Campus Minister or the Administrative Assistant for Campus Ministry.     Essential Duties and Responsibilities Recruitment, Programming, & Communication (60%) Actively recruit student participants for programs: Invite, advertise, promote, etc. Attend Campus Ministry events; capture digital images of events; lead prayers. Design, update and maintain CM social media presence and hard-copy flyers. Meet regularly with Campus Ministry professional staff and other Student Ministers to: Receive training and communicate about assigned tasks.  Plan and implement Campus Ministry programs. Coordinate efforts and ideas about communication and media presence. Coordinate calendars and upcoming events / needs Receive formation in basic principles of ministry Collaborate with other university departments on shared projects (e.g.: Residence Life; Athletics; Office of Student Engagement; Student Organizations.) Events Ambassador and Logistics Assistant ( 30%) Be an outgoing ambassador for CUH Campus Ministry with students, staff and prospective students in a professional and friendly manner. Greet and assist visitors to the Campus Ministry Office in a professional and friendly manner.  Prepare for and be present to represent Campus Ministry at campus events such as New Student Orientation, Opportunities Fair, Silversword Preview Day, Admitted Student Day, and similar events. Maintain supplies and storage areas; assist in preparations and set up for major Campus Ministry events. Assist with office tasks as needed: preparing powerpoint slides, photocopying, collating, organizing supplies, etc. Be service oriented: actively looking for ways to help staff and visitors Other Duties as Assigned/Needed (10%) Disclaimer This list of responsibilities is not exhaustive. Details relating to both essential and non-essential functions of the job are not precise and are only an approximation, which can vary on a day-to-day basis and are subject to change on an as-needed basis and/or in the sole discretion of supervisory management. Education and Experience Minimum Must be a currently enrolled Chaminade University student Preferred Student should maintain a current GPA of at least 3.0 Required Knowledge, Skills & Abilities  Ability to reach out to, engage and invite strangers in a friendly manner, for the sake of evangelizing and inviting others closer to Christ.  Ability and willingness to work on campus evenings and weekends. Excellent communication skills. Eagerness and comfort with engaging and inviting others. Proficiency with computer, social media, creating and editing digital photos, graphics and videos. Ability to organize, plan & execute duties and meet deadlines. Ability to work independently with minimal supervision. Attention to detail with a focus on thoroughness and quality. High integrity and ethical standards. Preferred Knowledge, Skill & Abilities Knowledge of and experience with planning and coordinating ministers for Catholic liturgies. Experience/familiarity with CUH Campus Ministry mission and events. Physical Requirements Duties involve light work in an office and community setting and requires a minimum of physical effort with intermittent sitting, standing, climbing stairs, and walking inclines. Must be able to lift 20 pounds, walk the campus with ease, and have excellent motor skills. Must have finger dexterity. Must be able to communicate information and ideas so that others will understand. Other Requirements:  This is a Part-time Non-Exempt Student Worker position. Depending on the project cycles and workflow demands of the department, additional hours or workday schedule changes may be occasionally required. Must be willing and able to work occasional nights and weekends and a varying schedule. Performs such similar, comparable or related duties as may be assigned or required. Observes all safety and health regulations and works in accordance with safe work procedures and policies of the University. Reports unsafe acts/conditions and injuries in a timely and proper manner The employee is expected to adhere to all University policies while employed. The policies can be found at https://chaminade.edu/compliance/resources/ or on the employee Share Portal Marianist Identity/Native Hawaiian & Pacific Island Serving:  An expressed willingness to respect and support the Catholic and Marianist identity of Chaminade University of Honolulu and to perform all duties in a manner consistent with Marianist educational values and mission of the University. Understanding of and respect for the University’s designation as an institution that serves students of Native Hawaiian and Pacific Island ancestry.",
      "department": ""
    },
