      "title": "Student Worker Chemistry Lab Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-04\n\nCHAMINADE UNIVERSITY OF HONOLULU     Position Information Title:  Student Worker, Chemistry Laboratory Assistant  Division:   School of Natural Sciences and Mathematics  Department:  Chemistry  Non-Exempt Part time   Position Summary The responsibilities of this position comprise of assisting the Professors in the laboratory.      Learning Outcomes  1. Proper setup and operation of laboratory equipment  2. Scientific communication skills  3. Critical thinking and problem-solving skills   4. Teamwork and student support skills    Reports to: Direct Report to: Hilary Corcoran  Indirect Report to: Dr. Chrystie Naeole & SNSM Faculty    Essential Duties and Responsibilities 1. Preparing the lab for daily exercises  2. Being present during lab to assist both the Professor and students  3. Cleaning glassware, materials, lab surfaces, etc. after the completion of lab exercises  4. Adhere to prescribed laboratory dress code 5. Other duties as assigned   Disclaimer This list of responsibilities is not exhaustive.  Details relating to both essential and non-essential functions of the job are not precise and are only an approximation, which can vary on a day-to-day basis and are subject to change on an as-needed basis and/or in the sole discretion of supervisory management.   Education and Experience   Minimum Current major in Biology, Biochemistry, Chemistry or Forensic Science with a minimum grade of B for CH/BC 203/L and CH/BC 204/L and a minimum cumulative GPA of 2.8.  Current major in Nursing with a minimum grade of B for BI 161/L and CH 254/L and a minimum cumulative GPA of 2.8.   Preferred Student should maintain a current GPA of at least 2.8   Required Knowledge, Skills & Abilities  Preparing for lab requires knowledge of solution preparation, supply location, scientific equipment operation and awareness of safety concerns in the lab exercise.  Work with hazardous materials may be involved so awareness of safety concerns in the lab is compulsory.   Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite or related software. Organized with meticulous attention to detail. Ability to prioritize work and resources. Ability to meet deadlines. Attention to detail with a focus on thoroughness and quality. High integrity and ethical standards.   Physical Requirements Duties involve light work in an office and community setting and requires a minimum of physical effort with intermittent sitting, standing, climbing stairs, and walking inclines. Must be able to lift  2 0 pounds, walk the campus with ease, and have excellent motor skills. Must have finger dexterity. Must be able to communicate information and ideas so that others will understand.   Other Requirements:  This is a Part-time Non-Exempt Student Worker position. Depending on the project cycles and workflow demands of the department, additional hours or workday schedule changes may be occasionally required.   Must be willing and able to work occasional nights and weekends and a varying schedule. Performs such similar, comparable or related duties as may be assigned or required.   Observes all safety and health regulations and works in accordance with safe work procedures and policies of the University. Reports unsafe acts/conditions and injuries in a timely and proper manner.  The employee is expected to adhere to all University policies while employed.  The policies can be found at https://chaminade.edu/compliance/resources/ or on the employee Share Portal.    Marianist Identity/Native Hawaiian & Pacific Island Serving:  An expressed willingness to respect and support the Catholic and Marianist identity of Chaminade University of Honolulu and to perform all duties in a manner consistent with Marianist educational values and mission of the University.  Understanding of and respect for the University’s designation as an institution that serves students of Native Hawaiian and Pacific Island ancestry.",
