      "title": "Professional Tutor and Academic Coach",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-31\n\nLocation: Honolulu\n\nChaminade University of Honolulu   Mission Statement Chaminade University offers its students an education in a collaborative learning environment that prepares them for life, service and successful careers. Guided by its Catholic, Marianist and liberal arts educational traditions, Chaminade encourages the development of moral character, personal competencies, and a commitment to build a just and peaceful society. The University offers both the civic and church communities of the Pacific region its academic and intellectual resources in the pursuit of common aims.   Position Information Title:  Professional Tutor and Academic Coach Division:  Enrollment Management and Student Success Department:  Kōkua ʻIke: Center for Student Learning Non-exempt, part-time   Department Information Description:  Kōkua ʻIke: Center for Student Learning is committed to supporting the success of all Chaminade students, whether undergraduate or graduate, and whether in person or online, by offering a reduced-distraction study space, Americans with Disabilities Act accommodations, and career, proctoring, and tutoring services. Location:  Kōkua ʻIke: Center for Student Learning   Reporting Relationships Direct Report:  Tutoring and Academic Coaching Services Coordinator Indirect Report:  Career Pathway and Success Coach   Essential Duties and Responsibilities Provide one-on-one or group tutoring and academic coaching sessions by appointment, either in person or online. Support students with course content, study strategies, SMART goals, and academic planning. Assist students with resumes and cover letters as needed. Foster a respectful, inclusive, and supportive environment for all students. Arrive on time and be prepared for all scheduled sessions. Maintain accurate records of each session, including notes and attendance. Check email regularly for appointment notifications and communications; all appointments are booked through Reservio and synced to Google Calendar. Communicate regularly with the Tutoring and Academic Coaching Services Coordinator and collaborate with fellow Tutors and Academic Coaches to ensure consistent, high-quality support. Participate in all required training sessions and workshops. Represent Kōkua ʻIke professionally in both in-person and online settings.   Disclaimer This list of responsibilities is not comprehensive. The details of both essential and non-essential job functions may vary from day to day. These responsibilities are subject to change as needed at the discretion of supervisory management.   Education and Experience Minimum Bachelor’s degree in relevant field Demonstrated ability to communicate and collaborate effectively with others Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines Proficiency or familiarity with digital design tools (e.g., Canva); Google products (e.g., Docs, Sheets, and Slides); and Microsoft products Commitment to equity-minded, inclusive, and student-centered services within a collaborative campus environment     Preferred Master’s degree in relevant field Experience with tutoring, academic coaching, or student success initiatives in a K-12 or higher education setting Experience working with Asian American, Pacific Islander, and local Hawai‘i student populations Proficiency or familiarity with Reservio or similar platforms   Physical Requirements This position may involve light physical activity in both indoor and outdoor settings. Successful candidates should be comfortable alternating between standing and sitting, as well as navigating stairs and sloped walkways. They should also be comfortable lifting and carrying up to 20 pounds. Strong motor skills and clear, effective communication are essential.   Other Requirements This is a part-time, non-exempt employment position. Successful candidates may work up to 19 hours per week; however, employment is on an as-needed basis . While the center's regular hours are Monday to Friday, 8:30 AM to 4:30 PM, excluding holidays, occasional early morning, evening, or weekend work may be required based on departmental needs. Flexibility and a willingness to adapt to a varied schedule are essential. Follow all health and safety regulations and university procedures. Promptly report any unsafe conditions, incidents, or injuries in accordance with established guidelines. Comply with all university policies and procedures, which are available at  https://chaminade.edu/compliance/resources  or through the employee SharePoint portal.   Catholic, Marianist Identity and Designation as a Native Hawaiian and Pacific Islander-Serving Institution An expressed willingness to respect and support the Catholic and Marianist identity of Chaminade University of Honolulu, and to perform all duties in a manner consistent with Marianist educational values and the University's mission. An understanding of and respect for the University's designation as an institution serving students of Native Hawaiian and Pacific Island ancestry.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=052b3ffb-78d8-40ac-bd43-f6ee902354e2&ccId=2543893806_3653&jobId=9206643829632_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Network and Systems Administrator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-29\n\nLocation: Honolulu\n\nCHAMINADE UNIVERSITY OF HONOLULU Chaminade University offers its students an education in a collaborative learning environment that prepares them for life, service and successful careers. Guided by its Catholic, Marianist and liberal arts educational traditions, Chaminade encourages the development of moral character, personal competencies, and a commitment to build a just and peaceful society. The University offers both the civic and church communities of the Pacific region its academic and intellectual resources in the pursuit of common aims Position Information Title: Network and Systems Administrator (Level 2 Support) Department: Information Technology & Services  Full Time, Exempt  Classification:  E/A/M II Position Summary Under the general supervision of the Senior Director of Information Technology Systems and Senior DevOps & Infrastructure Technical Lead, the Network Administrator (Level 2 Support) provides escalated technical support for the university's wired and wireless network infrastructure. This role resolves network and connectivity issues escalated from the IT Service Desk (Level 1 Support), performs routine network hardware and software maintenance, and assists with monitoring network performance, reliability, and security across campus and residence facilities. The Network Administrator works closely with the IT Service Desk team to troubleshoot escalated tickets, supports wireless connectivity for students, faculty, and staff, and helps maintain accurate documentation of network devices, configurations, and inventory. This role assists with the implementation of network security protocols and participates in network and cybersecurity planning under the direction of the Network Manager or Senior Director of Information Technology Systems. Working within established policies and procedures, this position performs network and computer hardware/software installation, maintenance, and troubleshooting with minimal to moderate supervision, escalating complex or unresolved issues to the Network Manager or Senior Director of Information Technology Systems. This position combines hands-on technical support with routine network administration responsibilities and includes project role outs for new/upgraded IT network hardware and software. Reports to Direct Report To: Network Manager or Senior Director of Information Technology Systems. Consolidated Role Responsibilities: Network Infrastructure & Maintenance Supports campus-wide network performance, reliability, and security, escalating complex or unresolved issues to the Senior Director of Information Technology Systems and Senior DevOps & Infrastructure Technical Lead. Performs routine network hardware and software maintenance, including configuration backups, patches, and security updates. Identifies network problems, determines root causes, and implements resolutions within the scope of the position. Helps ensure the uninterrupted function of essential networking services and equipment across campus and residence facilities. Help Desk & Technical Support (Level 2 Escalation) Provides second-tier (Level 2) technical support for network-related help desk tickets escalated from Level 1 Service Desk staff. Troubleshoots and resolves wired network port and connectivity issues for staff, faculty, and students. Mentors and provides guidance to Level 1 Service Desk staff on network-related troubleshooting techniques. Documents ticket resolutions and maintains accurate records within the ticketing system. Wireless Network Support Installs and maintains wireless access points, antennas, and related hardware and software for students, faculty, and staff. Monitors and troubleshoots wireless connectivity issues across campus. Creates and maintains a database and inventory of installed wireless devices. Security & Planning Assists in implementing and maintaining network security protocols, including endpoint protection and access controls. Participates in network planning and cybersecurity planning activities under the direction of the Network Manager or Senior Director of Information Technology Systems. Supports backup and disaster recovery procedures for network systems. Inventory & Vendor Coordination Maintains inventory of network equipment and orders supplies and repair or replacement parts as needed. Works with vendors to ensure network components are appropriate, assisting with installation and configuration when required. Assists with tracking warranties, licenses, and maintenance agreements for network hardware and software. Other Duties Performs other duties as assigned by the Senior Director of Information Technology Systems and Senior DevOps & Infrastructure Technical Lead. Disclaimer This list of responsibilities is not exhaustive. Details relating to both essential and non-essential functions of the job are not precise and are only an approximation, which can vary on a day-to-day basis and are subject to change on an as-needed basis and/or in the sole discretion of supervisory management. Education and Experience Minimum Minimum education. An associate's degree in MIS, Computer Science, or a related field (a combination of network certifications, relevant experience, and training may be substituted for the degree, i.e. CompTia A+, Network+, Security+). Minimum experience. Two (2) years of experience installing, maintaining, and troubleshooting network and computer hardware and software. Experience in an educational setting preferred.   Preferred Requires a good working knowledge of networking concepts and technical competence, along with the ability to interact positively with students, faculty, and staff who possess a wide range of educational and technical backgrounds. Ability to work within established policies with general supervision is essential. Strong communication skills and a customer-oriented approach are required. Technical skills. Broad knowledge of network technology, including LAN/WAN, TCP/IP, and Wi-Fi standards. Working knowledge of Cisco networking equipment, hardware, and software required. Knowledge of Active Directory and Windows Server is helpful. Familiarity with Palo Alto firewalls and VPNs is preferred. Relevant certifications (e.g., CompTIA Network+, Cisco CCNA) are desirable.  Physical Requirements This position requires the ability to traverse the campus, stoop, bend, and climb stairs to access network equipment in various locations. Must be able to lift approximately 10-20 pounds, have finger dexterity for keyboard and equipment use, and possess excellent motor skills. Must be able to communicate information and ideas so that others will understand. Other Requirements This is a full time, non-exempt position. Forty hours per week (M-F) will be the general rule. However, depending on the project cycles and workflow demands of the department, additional hours or workday schedule changes may be occasionally required. Must be willing and able to work occasional nights and weekends and have a varying schedule when required. Performs such similar, comparable or related duties as may be assigned or required. Observes all safety and health regulations and works in accordance with safe work procedures and policies of the University. Reports unsafe acts/conditions and injuries in a timely and proper manner. The employee is expected to adhere to all University policies while employed. The policies can be found at https://chaminade.edu/compliance/resources/ or on the employee Share Portal Employee must have U.S. Citizenship or currently obtain a work permit before applying. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship Marianist Identity/Native Hawaiian & Pacific Island Serving An expressed willingness to respect and support the Catholic and Marianist identity of Chaminade University of Honolulu and to perform all duties in a manner consistent with Marianist educational values and mission of the University. Understanding of and respect for the University’s designation as an institution that serves students of Native Hawaiian and Pacific Island ancestry",
      "department": ""
    }
  },
